<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Merya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Merya people, Merians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Merya were a Finnic people who lived in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> region around Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-pleshcheyevo">Lake Pleshcheyevo</a>, in the area of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostov">Rostov</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslavl">Yaroslavl</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Russian Primary Chronicle</a> names them among the tribes paying tribute to the Rus' in the 9th century. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> settled the region from the 10th century, they were gradually absorbed into the Russian population.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/merya.jpg" alt="Merya" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: merja.ru · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Volodimeriae_till_mid_12ht_century_neighbouring_Mariland,_Erzyaland_and_Miscaris.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
